I encoded the old rule independently as sequential capped withdrawals and the revised rule as a common capped fraction of stated needs. Across 205 nonnegative inlet values (0–20 in tenths plus points immediately above/below 8 and 12), both conserve all inlet water, never give negative delivery/onward flow, and never exceed the stipulated needs. Old W=8 yields U8/D0, W=12 yields U8/D4; dry6 yields old U6/D0 and revised U4/D2. The mean, two-day unmet amount, percentages and zero-loss reservoir arithmetic all check. No water is created by allocation, and moving needs between days is explicitly disallowed in this case.

